| Scheme | ok | n_parts | max \|S\| | colors | Notes |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
| `m68_intra_time_det_pack` | **0** | — | — | — | Transitive colocation collides inside parts (e.g. dets 0–3) |
| **`det_comp_paired`** | **1** | **16** | **7** | **7** | **Chosen** |
| `one_det` | 1 | 24 | 4 | 4 | Fallback; more context switches |

**Chosen construction:** Stim phenom DEM has **2** detector connected components (sizes 16, 8). Form part \(i\) from the \(i\)-th detector of each component (pad) + those detectors’ private boundaries. Guarantees ≤1 detector per component per part → Helios-feasible. Colors used **7 ≤ 16**.

**Implication:** M68’s n=6 pack remains valid for **Yosys resource** discussion only; it is **not** a legal Helios-n schedule partition under colocation. Prefer **N_CTX≥16** (chosen) for schedule RTL — update vs M69’s N_CTX≥6 hint.

